--- S2.1  Tournament census n=3..6: Hamiltonian paths h and |Aut| (vectorised DP) ---
  n=3:      8 labelled tournaments; h values = [1, 3] ; |Aut| values = [1, 3] ; max h = 3
  n=4:     64 labelled tournaments; h values = [1, 3, 5] ; |Aut| values = [1, 3] ; max h = 5
  n=5:   1024 labelled tournaments; h values = [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15] ; |Aut| values = [1, 3, 5] ; max h = 15
  n=6:  32768 labelled tournaments; h values = [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45] ; |Aut| values = [1, 3, 5, 9] ; max h = 45
  union of attained h for n<=6: [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45]
  odd values <= 45 NOT attained for n<=6: [7, 21, 35, 39]  (7 and 21 absent, as THM-1745 / death-star S70 state for all n; the others fill in at larger n per the theorem)
  Mersenne probe: 2^j-1 = [1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 63] ; attained for n<=6: [1, 3, 15, 31] ; max h per n vs 2^(n-1)-1: [(3, 3, 3), (4, 5, 7), (5, 15, 15), (6, 45, 31)]
  VERDICT (a): 7 = 2^3-1 has no Mersenne mechanism: the spectrum is 'odds minus {7,21}' so 1,3,15,31,63,... ARE attained;
      the max h at n=4 is 5 (< 7) and at n=5 it is 15 = 2^4-1 while 7 is skipped; 63 = 2^6-1 = 9*7 is in the spectrum (THM-1745 head).
      The row-braid fact ord_9(2)=6 (9 | 63) and the tournament hole 7 share the prime 7 only as a numeral: NO MAP FOUND.

